From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:29:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "FROMLIST: Bluetooth: hci_qca: Set
 'bt_en_available' based on W_DISABLE2# presence in M.2 connector"

This reverts commit 5b9e84dd13df3aa34a59235033b434efb5b675a1.

This was taken from an early posting of the M.2 Bluetooth pwrseq series,
where the decision was keyed off the presence of the w-disable2-gpios
property on the connector. Since v3 of the monza-wireless series that patch
was replaced by "Bluetooth: hci_qca: Set 'bt_en_available' based on pwrseq
power controllability", which uses the generic pwrseq_is_controllable() API
and also covers providers other than the M.2 connector. Revert the old
version so the upstream replacement can be applied as posted.

Signed-off-by: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [qcom-6.18.y specific: reverts an early version of a patch carried by that branch, superseded by the pwrseq controllability rework]
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index 086604ca2b48..ec0a6d9bf72e 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2469,17 +2469,10 @@ static int qca_serdev_probe(struct serdev_device *serdev)
 		 * the M.2 Key E connector.
 		 */
 		if (of_graph_is_present(dev_of_node(&serdev->ctrl->dev))) {
-			struct device *dev;
-
 			qcadev->bt_power->pwrseq = devm_pwrseq_get(&serdev->ctrl->dev,
 								   "uart");
 			if (IS_ERR(qcadev->bt_power->pwrseq))
 				return PTR_ERR(qcadev->bt_power->pwrseq);
-
-			dev = pwrseq_to_device(qcadev->bt_power->pwrseq);
-			if (!device_property_present(dev, "w-disable2-gpios"))
-				bt_en_available = false;
-
 			break;
 		}
 
